<% title "Payouts — #{@event.name}" %>

<%= render "events/nav", selected: :payouts %>

<h1 class="heading">Payouts</h1>

<%# Fuime: above everything, because a venture that cannot sell has a more
    urgent problem than how it gets paid. Renders nothing when clear. %>
<%= render "fuime/selling_blockers", event: @event %>

<%# Fuime: moving money out of the venture.

    Two audiences on one page, deliberately. The teen sees what they have and can
    ask for it; the responsible adult sees what they are being asked to approve.
    Neither gets the other's controls — a teen approving their own payout would
    defeat the ownership structure the whole company rests on (CLAUDE.md L2), and it
    is blocked in EventPolicy, in Fuime::PayoutService and in PayoutRequest.

    TWO SHAPES, and every piece of copy on this page depends on which one:

      * family venture — the guardian owns the Stripe account, so a payout is
        Stripe sending money to the guardian's own bank. `@school_settled` false.

      * school venture — the school owns one account for the whole programme, so
        Stripe cannot send this student's share to this student's own bank (see
        the AddDestinationToPayoutRequests migration). The school pays them and
        confirms it here. `@school_settled` true.

    The page previously assumed the first shape unconditionally and told school
    students to "ask my guardian" — a person who by design does not exist, on a
    request nobody but a Fuime admin could then approve.

    Plain markup on purpose (Milestone 4: correctness over beauty). %>

<% account = @connected_account %>

<%# FUIME: why money cannot leave, and the two models answer it differently.

    This block used to read `@connected_account` unconditionally. Under
    merchant-of-record that account does not exist and never will — the venture
    has no Stripe account, because Fuime is the seller — so `account.blank?` was
    permanently true and every operator was told "a parent or guardian needs to
    set up this venture's payment account first", linking to a Connect
    onboarding screen MoR has retired. Right sentence, wrong model, and it sent
    people to a page that could not help them.

    Under MoR the real gates are a verified payout destination and a guardian,
    and they come from Event#payout_setup_blockers, which is the same list
    Fuime::PayableAssessment refuses a payout run on. One source, so the page and
    the run cannot tell an operator different things. %>
<% if Fuime::Features.merchant_of_record? %>
  <% payout_blockers = @event.payout_setup_blockers %>
  <% if payout_blockers.any? %>
    <%= render "application/callout", type: "warning", title: "Money can't be sent out yet" do %>
      <ul class="mb-0">
        <% payout_blockers.each do |blocker| %>
          <li><%= blocker %></li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
      <%# The destination is the half the operator can fix themselves, so it gets
          the link. The guardian half has no button — it is somebody accepting an
          invite — and a link implying otherwise would be a dead end. %>
      <p class="mb-0 mt1">
        <%= link_to "Set where your money goes", fuime_payout_method_path(event_slug: @event.slug), class: "underline" %>.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% elsif account.blank? || !account.ready_for_payouts? %>
  <%= render "application/callout", type: "warning", title: "Money can't be sent out yet" do %>
    <p class="mb-0">
      <% if account.blank? %>
        <% if @event.institutionally_sponsored? %>
          The school needs to set up this programme's payment account first.
          <%= link_to "See payment setup", fuime_payment_setup_path(event_slug: @event.slug), class: "underline" %>.
        <% else %>
          A parent or guardian needs to set up this venture's payment account first.
          They will own that account, and payouts go to their bank.
          <%= link_to "See payment setup", fuime_payment_setup_path(event_slug: @event.slug), class: "underline" %>.
        <% end %>
      <% else %>
        <%= account.status_description %>
        <%= link_to "See payment setup", fuime_payment_setup_path(event_slug: @event.slug), class: "underline" %>.
      <% end %>
    </p>
  <% end %>
<% end %>

<%# ── Earnings, not a balance ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

    This heading and the figure under it carry the legal distinction the
    merchant-of-record model rests on, so neither is free to be reworded casually.

    Fuime LLC is the seller of record: a customer pays Fuime for a sale Fuime made,
    that money is Fuime's own revenue, and this operator is a vendor Fuime pays on a
    fixed cadence. What they hold is a RECEIVABLE — an amount owed, payable on a
    stated date. What they do not hold is a balance on deposit, because a stored
    balance its holder withdraws at will is a deposit, and taking deposits without a
    charter is the one thing Fuime cannot do (CLAUDE.md L1/L5).

    So: "Fuime owes you $84.20, paid on Friday 14 August." Never "your balance",
    and never a Withdraw button against a sum held indefinitely. Every figure below
    comes from Fuime::PayablesLedger, which is the only thing an operator-facing
    view may ask — spec/views/fuime/payables_copy_spec.rb enforces that. %>

<h2 class="mt2">Your earnings</h2>

<p class="h1 mt0 mb1"><%= render_money(@payables.amount_owed_cents) %></p>

<p class="secondary mt0"><%= @payables.owed_sentence %></p>

<%# Repeated here, not only on the offers page. This is the screen an operator
    opens when a number has changed, and "Refunds and disputes" below is a row that
    needs an explanation next to it rather than in another tab. %>
<%= render "fuime/operator_sale_terms", event: @event %>

<% if @payables.pending_sales_cents.positive? %>
  <p class="secondary mt0">
    <%# Deliberately a separate sentence from the figure above, and never added to
        it. Money Stripe has taken but not released is coming, not owed today —
        merging the two is how a reader concludes Fuime is holding a balance for
        them. %>
    A further <strong><%= render_money(@payables.pending_sales_cents) %></strong>
    from recent sales hasn't been released by Stripe yet. It usually takes a couple
    of days, and it'll be included once it lands.
  </p>
<% end %>

<%# The breakdown. Present on the page rather than behind a link because "why is
    this smaller than my sales?" is the first question anyone asks, and the answer
    involves two different companies taking two different cuts.

    #breakdown always sums to the net payable by construction — the last row is a
    residual, not a category — so these figures cannot fail to add up. %>
<details class="mb2">
  <summary class="pointer">How this is worked out</summary>

  <table class="table--autosize mt1">
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Sales</td>
        <td class="right-align"><%= render_money(@payables.gross_sales_cents) %></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Fuime's fee</td>
        <td class="right-align">&minus;<%= render_money(@payables.fuime_fee_cents) %></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <%# Stripe's cut is itemised separately from Fuime's on purpose: they are
            two different companies taking two different amounts, and a family
            reconciling their books needs to see which is which. %>
        <td>Card processing (Stripe)</td>
        <td class="right-align">&minus;<%= render_money(@payables.processing_fee_cents) %></td>
      </tr>
      <% if @payables.refunds_cents.positive? %>
        <tr>
          <td>Refunds and disputes</td>
          <td class="right-align">&minus;<%= render_money(@payables.refunds_cents) %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
      <% if @payables.card_spend_cents.positive? %>
        <tr>
          <td>Spent on your Fuime card</td>
          <td class="right-align">&minus;<%= render_money(@payables.card_spend_cents) %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
      <% if @payables.committed_cents.positive? %>
        <tr>
          <td>Pending card holds</td>
          <td class="right-align">&minus;<%= render_money(@payables.committed_cents) %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
      <% if @payables.paid_out_cents.positive? %>
        <tr>
          <td>Already paid to you</td>
          <td class="right-align">&minus;<%= render_money(@payables.paid_out_cents) %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
      <% unless @payables.other_adjustments_cents.zero? %>
        <tr>
          <%# The residual. Named vaguely because it genuinely is "everything else"
              — school awards, corrections, anything posted by a path that predates
              the ledger key scheme. Shown rather than hidden so the rows always
              reconcile to the total. %>
          <td>Other adjustments</td>
          <td class="right-align"><%= render_money(@payables.other_adjustments_cents) %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Owed to you</strong></td>
        <td class="right-align"><strong><%= render_money(@payables.net_payable_cents) %></strong></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</details>

<p class="secondary mt0"><em><%= @payables.disclosure %></em></p>

<%# What Stripe can move TODAY, which is a different question from what is owed.
    Shown only when it disagrees with the payables figure or cannot be read at all,
    because on the ordinary day the two match and a second number would just invite
    the reader to wonder which one is theirs. %>
<% if @available_cents.nil? %>
  <p class="secondary mt0">
    <%# Not the same as zero, and must not be shown as zero. A teen told they have
        $0 when Fuime simply could not reach Stripe will conclude their money is
        gone. The figure above still stands — what Fuime owes does not depend on
        Stripe answering. %>
    We can't reach Stripe right now, so we can't confirm what can be sent today.
    This doesn't change what you're owed.
  </p>
<% elsif @available_cents < @payables.amount_owed_cents %>
  <p class="secondary mt0">
    Of that, <strong><%= render_money(@available_cents) %></strong> can be sent
    today — money from a sale takes a couple of days to clear before it can move.
  </p>
<% end %>

<% if @pending_request.present? %>
  <%= render "application/callout", type: "info",
                                    title: "#{number_to_currency(@pending_request.amount)} waiting for approval" do %>
    <p>
      Requested by <strong><%= @pending_request.requested_by.name.presence || @pending_request.requested_by.email %></strong>
      on <%= @pending_request.created_at.strftime("%B %-d, %Y") %>.
      <% if @pending_request.destination_note.present? %>
        <br>
        To be sent to: <strong><%= @pending_request.destination_note %></strong>
      <% end %>
    </p>

    <% if @can_decide %>
      <%# The adult's decision. Both buttons are here rather than the reject being
          hidden behind a second page, because someone who cannot easily say no will
          say nothing, and a request that sits forever is worse for the teen than a
          decline with a reason. %>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start" style="gap: 1rem;">
        <% if @pending_request.personal_transfer? %>
          <%= button_to "Approve",
                        fuime_payout_approve_path(event_slug: @event.slug, id: @pending_request.id),
                        method: :post,
                        class: "btn bg-success",
                        data: { turbo_confirm: "Approve paying #{number_to_currency(@pending_request.amount)} " \
                                               "to #{@pending_request.requested_by.first_name}? " \
                                               "You'll mark it as paid once the school has sent it."
} %>
        <% else %>
          <%= button_to "Approve and send",
                        fuime_payout_approve_path(event_slug: @event.slug, id: @pending_request.id),
                        method: :post,
                        class: "btn bg-success",
                        data: { turbo_confirm: "Send #{number_to_currency(@pending_request.amount)} to your bank account?" } %>
        <% end %>

        <%= form_with url: fuime_payout_reject_path(event_slug: @event.slug, id: @pending_request.id),
                      method: :post, class: "flex items-start", style: "gap: 0.5rem;" do |f| %>
          <%= f.text_field :rejection_reason,
                           placeholder: "Reason (optional)",
                           aria: { label: "Reason for declining" } %>
          <%= f.submit "Decline", class: "btn bg-error" %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% else %>
      <p class="mb-0">
        <% if @school_settled %>
          <%# No guardian exists on a school venture, and the old copy sent the
              student to a guardian-invite page that would never resolve this. %>
          Waiting on the school to approve it.
        <% else %>
          <% guardians = @event.overseeing_guardians %>
          <% if guardians.any? %>
            Waiting on <strong><%= guardians.map { |g| g.name.presence || g.email }.to_sentence %></strong>
            to approve it.
          <% else %>
            There's no active guardian on this venture yet, so nobody can approve it.
            <%= link_to "Invite your guardian", new_guardianship_path, class: "underline" %>.
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </p>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% elsif @can_request %>
  <h2 class="mt2"><%= @school_settled ? "Take money out" : "Request a payout" %></h2>

  <%= form_with url: fuime_payouts_create_path(event_slug: @event.slug), method: :post do |f| %>
    <div class="field">
      <%= f.label :amount, "Amount", class: "bold" %>
      <%= f.text_field :amount,
                       placeholder: "0.00",
                       inputmode: "decimal",
                       autocomplete: "off" %>
    </div>

    <% if @school_settled %>
      <div class="field">
        <%= f.label :destination_note, "Where should it go?", class: "bold" %>
        <%# Free text, and no bank fields anywhere. The school already has whatever
            details it needs to pay a student it enrolled; Fuime collecting a
            minor's account number to hand back to them would be a store of exactly
            the data CLAUDE.md L4 says not to hold, for no capability at all. %>
        <%= f.text_field :destination_note,
                         placeholder: "e.g. my own bank account",
                         autocomplete: "off" %>
        <p class="secondary mb0">
          Just a note for the school — don't put your account number here. They'll
          use the details they already have on file.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="secondary">
        The school has to approve this, and then pays you the same way it pays
        anyone. The money is held in the school's account, so Fuime doesn't send it
        and never holds it.
      </p>

      <%= f.submit "Ask the school", class: "btn bg-accent" %>
    <% else %>
      <p class="secondary">
        Your guardian has to approve this before any money moves. It goes to their
        bank account, not to Fuime.
      </p>

      <%= f.submit "Ask my guardian", class: "btn bg-accent" %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <% if @school_settled %>
    <p class="secondary">
      You don't have to take it out. Anything you leave here stays in the venture
      and you can spend it on the business.
    </p>
  <% end %>
<% elsif @can_decide %>
  <p class="secondary">
    There's nothing waiting for you to approve. When
    <%= @event.name %> asks for a payout, it will show up here.
  </p>
<% end %>

<% if @unsettled_requests.present? && @unsettled_requests.any? %>
  <h2 class="mt2">Approved, not yet paid</h2>

  <%# The business office's to-do list. Distinct from History because the ledger has
      NOT been debited yet: the debit waits for someone to assert the money actually
      went, so an approved-but-unpaid transfer is still owed to the operator. %>
  <table class="table--autosize">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Approved</th>
        <th>Amount</th>
        <th>To</th>
        <% if @can_settle %><th></th><% end %>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% @unsettled_requests.each do |request| %>
        <tr>
          <td><%= request.approved_at&.strftime("%b %-d, %Y") %></td>
          <td><%= number_to_currency(request.amount) %></td>
          <td>
            <%= request.requested_by.name.presence || request.requested_by.email %>
            <% if request.destination_note.present? %>
              <span class="secondary">— <%= request.destination_note %></span>
            <% end %>
          </td>
          <% if @can_settle %>
            <td>
              <%= button_to "Mark as paid",
                            fuime_payout_settle_path(event_slug: @event.slug, id: request.id),
                            method: :post,
                            class: "btn bg-success",
                            data: { turbo_confirm: "Confirm the school has sent " \
                                                   "#{number_to_currency(request.amount)} to " \
                                                   "#{request.requested_by.first_name}? " \
                                                   "This takes it off what Fuime owes them."
} %>
            </td>
          <% end %>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
<% end %>

<h2 class="mt2">History</h2>

<% if @history.empty? %>
  <p class="secondary">No payout requests yet.</p>
<% else %>
  <table class="table--autosize">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Requested</th>
        <th>Amount</th>
        <th>Status</th>
        <th>Decided by</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% @history.each do |request| %>
        <tr>
          <td><%= request.created_at.strftime("%b %-d, %Y") %></td>
          <td><%= number_to_currency(request.amount) %></td>
          <td>
            <%# Each state gets its own sentence rather than the raw aasm_state,
                because "failed" on its own tells a family nothing about whether
                they still have the money. They do — Stripe returns it.

                "approved" means two different things on the two paths: Stripe has
                already sent it, or a school still owes it. Showing "Sent to your
                bank" for the second would be a straight falsehood. %>
            <% case request.aasm_state
               when "pending" %>
              <span class="badge bg-info">Waiting for approval</span>
            <% when "approved" %>
              <% if request.personal_transfer? %>
                <span class="badge bg-info">Approved — school is paying it</span>
              <% else %>
                <span class="badge bg-info">Sent to your bank</span>
              <% end %>
            <% when "paid" %>
              <span class="badge bg-success">
                <%= request.personal_transfer? ? "Paid to you" : "Arrived" %>
              </span>
            <% when "rejected" %>
              <span class="badge bg-muted">Declined</span>
              <% if request.rejection_reason.present? %>
                <span class="secondary">— <%= request.rejection_reason %></span>
              <% end %>
            <% when "failed" %>
              <span class="badge bg-error">Didn't go through</span>
              <span class="secondary">
                — <%= request.failure_message.presence || "Stripe couldn't send it." %>
                It's been added back to what you're owed.
              </span>
            <% end %>
          </td>
          <td>
            <% if request.approved_by.present? %>
              <%= request.approved_by.name.presence || request.approved_by.email %>
              <% if request.settled_by.present? && request.settled_by_id != request.approved_by_id %>
                <span class="secondary">— paid by <%= request.settled_by.name.presence || request.settled_by.email %></span>
              <% end %>
            <% else %>
              <span class="muted">—</span>
            <% end %>
          </td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
<% end %>

<%# Standing disclosure. Fuime is not a bank and never holds this money — on a
    family venture the connected account and the bank account are both the
    guardian's; on a school venture they are both the school's (L5). %>
<p class="secondary mt2">
  <% if @school_settled %>
    This venture's money is held in the school's own Stripe account, and the school
    pays students from it. Fuime is a financial technology company, not a bank, and
    never holds this money.
  <% else %>
    Payouts are sent by Stripe from the venture's own account to the bank account
    the parent or guardian connected. Fuime is a financial technology company, not a
    bank, and never holds this money.
  <% end %>
</p>
